 claim to be stranded  it doesn't take long for his dalliance  to come back to haunt him when the women  are revealed to be more than they  originally seemed  then on november 12th horror devotees  have 2008's prom night to look forward  to  loosely based on the 1980 film starring  jamie lee curtis the 2008 feature  centers around donna  a traumatized teen who witnessed her  teacher violently slay her entire family  after he became obsessed with her three  years later he escaped from prison just  in time to ruin donna senior prom  with another killing spree november 2020  selection of dramas on netflix is packed  with star-studded movies starring  michael b  jordan joseph gordon-levitt and amy  adams whether you're looking to catch up  on past hits or check out something  entirely new there truly is something  for every drama lover on netflix next  month the streamer is kicking things off  with 2016 snowden which arrives on  november 1st  directed by oliver stone the film  dramatizes the life of edward snowden  as he trades in a job within the  intelligence community to become a  whistleblowing fugitive  then on november 12th movie fans can  revisit foodvale station  the first feature-length film helmed by  black panther director ryan coogler  the heartbreaking film is based on a  true story and stars michael b  jordan as oscar grant a young black man  who was killed during an encounter with  police  just a few days later on november 16th  viewers can stream another acclaimed  drama movie based on a true story  2016's loving starring joel edgerton and  ruth nager  as richard and mildred loving the couple  who successfully challenged state laws  that banned interracial marriages  nager's incredible performance in loving  earned her a best actress nomination  at the 2017 oscars finally on november  24th  the long-awaited hillbilly elegy arrives  on netflix based on jd vance's  best-selling memoir of the same name the  film focuses on a struggling  working-class family  in the appalachia region of the united  states and their yale graduate son who  was forced to return to his dying  hometown  to help his family the movie's cast is  headed up by the heavy-hitting duo of  amy adams and glenn close  which may make this one appealing  whether you've read the book before or  not  everyone in this world is one of three  kinds good terminator  a bad terminator and neutral  netflix is bringing a cornucopia of  action to its digital shelves in  november 2020.  for anyone still reeling from the end of  season two cobra kai fans will be  thrilled to learn that there's another  shot of miyagi dough  coming to their device of choice this  1994 follow-up to the original karate  kid trilogy  sees mr miyagi taking on a new student  julie played by hilary swank  it was a simpler time back when movies  about hillary swank learning how to  fight didn't end with clint eastwood  taking her off life support  additionally the 2018 mark wahlberg  starring action thriller mile 22  brought to you by director peter berg  the guy behind hancock and battleship  drops on the streaming service on  november 1st netflix is also offering to  subscribers a pair of dystopian flicks  next month  a clockwork orange stanley kubrick's  owed to milk and long johns will be  available to stream beginning november  1st  that was a real kick and good for laughs  and lashings of the old  ultra violent looking for a double  feature try pairing a clockwork orange  with v for vendetta  which you can queue up starting on  november 15th  ready to learn something new netflix has  a variety of documentaries heading to  his library in november 2020  all designed to help you become more  informed about current events music  and the latest true crime mystery this  month kicks off on november 5th with  carmel who killed maria mata  the new ducky series dives into the  mystery surrounding the death of maria  marta garcia belsunce who's at the  center of a case that sparked an outcry  in